            <div xml:id="d710">

                <pb facs="0809" n="716" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg716"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.516/340: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chapin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-28T13:00:00-05:00">March 28, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. My telegram No. 22, March 28, 10 a.m. Chamber of Deputies passed bill of
                    sanction for bank purchase contract this morning by unanimous vote. I am
                    reliably informed that text is the same as that passed by Senate yesterday.</p>
                <pb facs="0810" n="717" xml:id="pg717"/>
                <p>I respectfully request contents of this and No. 22 be communicated to Armour at
                    Princeton.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
